    "title": "Police: Man threatened girls, viewed obscene photos at Benson Boone concert - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sarah Bawden No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nBOSTON (WPRI) — An 80-year-old Brookline man was arrested earlier after threatening and looking at obscene photos near two young girls at a concert in Boston earlier this week, according to authorities.\nAlan Musson has been charged with threat to commit a crime, disorderly conduct and disseminating obscene matter to a minor.\nMusson was taken into custody at the TD Garden Tuesday night during a Benson Boone concert, according to a police report obtained by WCVB .\nPolice said Musson started yelling at the two girls sitting behind him because they were cheering for the artist.\nThe two girls continued cheering, to which Musson turned around again and told them, “I will kill you,” according to police.\nPolice said the victims could also see Musson looking at inappropriate photos on the Grindr app from their seats.\nThe girls alerted security and were moved to different seats. Police said Musson admitted he was looking at a picture of a “naked guy” on his phone when officers questioned him about the incident.\nMusson is slated to face a judge on Thursday.\nDownload the WPRI 12 and Pinpoint Weather 12 apps to get breaking news and weather alerts.\nWatch 12 News Now on WPRI.com or with the free WPRI 12+ TV app .\nFollow us on social media:\nClose Thanks for signing up!\nWatch for us in your inbox.\nSubscribe Now\nDaily Roundup Copyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WPRI.com.",
